---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import Breadcrumbs from "../components/Breadcrumbs.astro";
import { SITE, authors } from "../lib/blog-data.js";
---

<BaseLayout
  title={`About - ${SITE.name}`}
  description={`About ${SITE.name}: A digital recollection of my ramblings`}
  canonical="/about"
>
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-5 py-12">
    <Breadcrumbs items={[{ label: "Home", to: "/" }, { label: "About" }]} />

    <header class="mt-6">
      <div class="text-xs font-medium uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-primary">About</div>
      <h1 class="mt-2 font-serif text-5xl font-semibold leading-[1.05]">
        A place for the great escape from online echo chambers.
      </h1>
    </header>

    <div class="prose-article mt-10">
      <p>
        Sometimes the constant bombardment of social media and our afflictions in life lead us to escape to a place distant from these conundrums. {SITE.name} began as a little project of mine where I could share my thoughts and my progress in the field of tech and life.
      </p>
      <p>
        Topics may diverge, consistency is not a promise, but you have to excuse me for that. Trust me, I try my best.
      </p>
      <p>
        I always remember this in my mind,
      </p>
      <h2>Act > Think</h2>
    </div>

    <section class="mt-12 border-t border-border pt-10">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-2xl font-semibold">Author</h2>
      <div class="mt-6 grid gap-6 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3">
        {
          authors.map((author) => (
            <a href={`/authors/${author.slug}`} class="group flex items-start gap-3">
              <img src={author.avatar} alt="" width="48" height="48" class="h-12 w-12 rounded-full" />
              <div>
                <div class="font-serif text-base font-semibold group-hover:text-primary">{author.name}</div>
                <div class="mt-1 text-sm text-muted-foreground">Lifelong learner</div>
              </div>
            </a>
          ))
        }
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
